<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <parent>
        <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
        <artifactId>kompile-app-parent</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>kompile-app-mcp</artifactId>
    <name>Kompile App - MCP Integration</name>
    <description>
        The MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration domain extracted from kompile-app-main's services
        package (ai.kompile.app.services.mcp): MCP server/client runtimes, the REST/stdio bridges and
        external-server manager, tool discovery/definition/permission, response compressors, and the
        MCP action log. Verified to reference nothing in app-main's services except ServerPortService
        (now in kompile-app-platform) — the small self-contained ToolCallWriterService (tool-call audit
        writer) moves in with it. Depends on app-core + platform + the filesystem/rag tool modules + the
        Spring-AI MCP client/server starters + embedded Jetty for the REST bridge. Package name preserved.
        See docs/architecture/services-decomposition-spec.md.

        The MCP *server* itself (ai.kompile.app.mcp: McpToolRegistry, McpServerConfig, the SSE
        transport and its /mcp controller) moved here from kompile-app-main when web-admin was carved
        out. It has to live below the persona web layers: kompile-app-web-chat and
        kompile-app-web-crawl now own the @Tool classes for their surfaces, and those tools are
        unreachable unless the app mounting them also has a server to expose them on. Leaving the
        server in app-main would have meant only the admin app speaks MCP.
        See docs/architecture/app-persona-boundary.md.
    </description>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
            <artifactId>kompile-app-core</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
            <artifactId>kompile-app-platform</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
            <artifactId>kompile-tool-filesystem</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
            <artifactId>kompile-tool-rag</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- McpToolRegistry runs every tool call past the gateway before dispatching. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>ai.kompile</groupId>
            <artifactId>kompile-tool-gateway</artifactId>
            <version>${project.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Spring-AI MCP client + webmvc server -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.ai</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-ai-starter-mcp-client</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.ai</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-ai-starter-mcp-server-webmvc</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Embedded Jetty for the REST MCP bridge -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.eclipse.jetty</groupId>
            <artifactId>jetty-server</artifactId>
            <version>11.0.20</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.eclipse.jetty</groupId>
            <artifactId>jetty-servlet</artifactId>
            <version>11.0.20</version>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</project>
